Rule 0
When you write a raise ValueError, put the message in a msg variable

Instead of:
raise ValueError("Some message")

You should do:
msg = "Some message"
raise ValueError(msg)



Rule 1
I often write functions like:

def my_function(...):
    """
    Some big docstring explaining stuff
    """
    ...

I might do some minor code but a common pattern I'm using is just to leave the function
empty and just tell an AI agent to fill if for me. If I point you to a function and you
fill it, if you create other sub-functions, start their docstrings with:

AI GENERATED FUNCTION

So that later on we can clean up confusion. You will only do this if I only select one
function to fill and I tell you to implement it. For other cases, you will not do this





Rule 2
Don't write dots at the end of the docstrings in python functions
This is to avoid using too many tokens and adding unnecessary noise to the file
